# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# The Content Security Policy deliberately lives in a <meta> tag inside each
# page rather than here. Cloudflare merges every matching rule in this file
# instead of overriding, so a path-specific rule cannot relax a site-wide
# one: the browser enforces the intersection and the strictest policy wins.
# A per-page meta tag is the only way to have a strict policy everywhere and
# a slightly looser one on the editor, which needs Google's sign-in script.
#
# Consequence: every page must carry its own CSP meta tag. If you add a page,
# copy the meta block from a sibling.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
